KiteImage
Copyright 2026 yuroyami

This product is a from-scratch, clean-room Kotlin Multiplatform reimplementation of
established image formats. The PNG inflate path derives from Mark Adler's
public-domain `puff` reference (vendored from KiteArchive, via the KiteTorrent /
libtorrent lineage).

Format references consulted for porting (study only, not redistributed; see
reference/REFERENCES.md) are each under permissive licenses: stb_image /
stb_image_write (public domain / MIT), lodepng (zlib), Apache Commons Imaging
(Apache-2.0).

Several codecs were written from their published specification rather than
ported from any source tree, and verified against a reference binary used only
as a test oracle: WebP lossless and the WebP container (Google's WebP specs;
checked against libwebp's cwebp/dwebp, BSD-3-Clause, neither read nor
redistributed), APNG (Mozilla's APNG specification), and the TIFF and BMP
feature sets added on top of the ported baselines (TIFF 6.0, Microsoft DIB
documentation).

AVIF and HEIC are deliberately excluded: AV1/HEVC decoders are beyond a realistic
pure-Kotlin port, and HEVC carries patent-licensing baggage besides.
